KNOWNBUG: N5008 [temp.deduct.call] + [dcl.fct]/2 + [temp.variadic]/5 -- a
free function template whose trailing return type is
`decltype(::new((void*)0) _Tp(declval<_Args>()...))` (the C++20
std::construct_at declaration) fails argument deduction with two or more
arguments constructing a class-template instance ("found no match for
symbol 'construct_at'").  The plain-return flavour of the identical body
works (cpp11_construct_at_pack_args); the trailing-return decltype over a
pack-expanded new-expression is the residual.  This is the remaining
front-end blocker of cpp20_map_basic (the C++20 headers route std::map
node construction through this exact construct_at declaration).  Flip to
CORE when the trailing-return decltype over a pack-expanded
new-expression is deduced.  g++/clang++ runtime-verified.
